# Bookstore (Django)

A book catalog web app built with Python and Django. Users can register, log in, and add, edit and delete their own books. A read-only REST API exposes the catalog.

> The templates are intentionally minimal and unstyled. This project focuses on backend logic: authentication, permissions, validation and a REST API.

## Features

- User registration, login and logout (custom views)
- Add, edit and delete books
- Ownership permissions: you can only edit or delete the books you added
- Form validation with error messages for empty fields
- Book detail page
- Django admin panel to manage users and books
- Read-only REST API built with Django REST Framework

## Tech Stack

- Python, Django
- Django REST Framework
- SQLite
- Django templates (HTML)

## Data Model

`Book`: title, author, year, rating, description, and `posted_by` (foreign key to the user who added it).

## API Endpoints (read-only)

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/` | List of available endpoints |
| GET | `/api/books/` | List all books |
| GET | `/api/books/<id>/` | Get a single book |

